                        "review": "This game gave me mixed thoughts. I'll try to elaborate more...\r\n\r\nThe reviews sounded off due its bugs and inability to complete the game, which made me skeptical - but  not enough to put it away. Starting the game, I found that it was OK, for a point and click adventure with a S.A.W style storyline. \r\n\r\nThe interface was a bit clunky but workable. The mouse veered off randomly and it gave me a headache - especially during the times when you have to chase/keep off the character on screen. The puzzles are good - but the interface and mouse handling screwed it up bad at times. There are many mini-games within the game, but I won't recommend playing them because I found them too finicky. \r\n\r\nImposing resource optimization by checking for batteries is neat, but only limited to batteries. The story has potential, but without sufficient backstory, it just falls flat. If you watched the usual stock of slasher movies, you'd be able to figure out the killer right away.\r\n\r\nWhich brings me to the secret ending (or sort of). It just doesn't fit with the rest of the story - at all. The other 4 endings fit in just fine. The secret ending could have instead given a bit more backstory on the killer's beginning.\r\n\r\nThe achievements are easy enough and you can get them in a single playthrough. At the end, I did not fully enjoy the experience, but it wasn't too bad either. It tilts more towards tolerable and so I'll recommend this game, but only if you have in your library and you're on a completion spree.\r\n\r\n- 5/10",
